// =======================================================================================
// The ten locales of tier one — решение 93, task Т-28-3.
// =======================================================================================
//
// ⚠ **The code page governs these ten exactly as it governs the two above**, and here it is
// load-bearing in ten alphabets at once: Cyrillic, Greek, the carons of Czech, the ogoneks of
// Polish, the dotless ı of Turkish. `#pragma code_page(65001)` above the tables is what makes
// them survive `rc.exe`, and the damage it prevents is silent — mojibake builds green and
// tests green until somebody looks at the window. The instrument that watches for it is
// `scratchpad-Э28\мохибейк-греп.ps1`, and it is run after every one of these blocks.
//
// ⚠ Every string here obeys `scratchpad-Э28\глоссарий.md`: one agreed word per term per
// language, decided **before** the first translation was written. A translation that reads
// well but names a term differently from the glossary is a defect of the translation.
//
// ⚠ «Lang Switcher» is not translated in any of the twelve — the decision on question 7.
// Neither are the key names (`Esc`, `Ctrl`, `Alt`, `Shift`, `F12`, `Pause`) or `%APPDATA%`.
// `{0}`, `{1}`, `{2}` keep their number and their count; only their place may move.
//
// The order below is the order of the language combo box, which is `Language::ALL`.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Ukrainian — `[general] language = "uk"`. LANG_UKRAINIAN 0x22.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LANGUAGE 0x22, 0x01
STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOG_CAPTION      "Lang Switcher — налаштування"
    IDS_GROUP_GENERAL       "Загальні"
    IDS_AUTOSTART           "Запускати під час входу в систему"
    IDS_LANGUAGE_LABEL      "Мова інтерфейсу:"
